  "classification": "defect",
  "status": "suspected",
  "description": "model_diff.py defers module loading without checking can_defer_load, allowing sliced weight construction to copy unread storage.",
  "trigger": "A compared module cannot defer: a sliced Linear or multi-slice GatedMLP, using eligible deferred mt_fread weights. The normal split threshold is 55,296. Issue 38 identifies a DeciLMForCausalLM checkpoint with an eight-way sliced MLP (49,920 versus 399,360). Such a registered model exists; at this revision unquantized loading fails earlier on the padding mismatch. No local execution or continuous affected range established.",
  "expected_behavior": "Respect module.can_defer_load before entering deferred loading, as the model loaders do.",
  "actual_behavior": "The comparison script brackets every module. LinearFP16 constructs a copied slice before queued reads populate the original weight, so the retained slice can contain uninitialised values. The unread-copy consequence is masked by the earlier unquantized padding mismatch for the model reported in issue 38.",
  "introductions": [
